Dear Lesley,

I hope you are doing fine.

For my student UK visa, I need a to have a letter of confirmation from an official financial sponsor.
Of course, it is a pure formality, but it can not come from a physical person, it should come from an international company or organization.

The letter should be addressed to the UK Border Agency in Paris, and here are the requirements:
"The letter must be on the organisation's official letter-headed paper or stationery, and must bear the organisation's official stamp. It must show:
- your name;
- course name: Mint Art, Style and Design, sponsored by University of Glasgow;
- the name and financial sponsor's name and contact details;
- the date of the letter - Today's date;
- the amount of money that the official financial sponsor is giving to you - statement that it will cover all of your course fees and living costs."

Would you be so kind to do this letter for me, on the behalf of one of Jeffrey's organizations? Please contact me for any detail!

Thank you so much for your help!!

